---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../site';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of use"
  description="Terms for using acqi.tech and the product preview. Product licensing is governed by a separate order."
>
  <section class="article-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="micro micro--red mb-1">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
      <div class="article-head__meta">
        <span class="micro">Last updated 17 November 2026</span>
        <span class="micro">Website and preview only</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <div class="note">
          <p>
            <strong>Status.</strong> ACQI Technologies is in formation. These terms are made
            between you and the founders trading as ACQI Technologies. They will be replaced by
            the incorporated entity's terms on incorporation, on substantially the same basis.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>1. Scope</h2>
        <p>
          These terms govern your use of the website at acqi.tech and the product preview behind
          its gate. They do not govern the ACQI product. Use of the product is governed by the
          licence and order signed with the customer.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What the site is</h2>
        <p>
          The site describes a product and the services around it. Descriptions are written to be
          accurate as at the date on the page, but they are not a specification and must not be
          relied on as one. The specification for a deployment is the statement of work signed
          for that deployment.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where the site states that something is planned, in development, partial or not held,
          that statement is deliberate and does not become a commitment to deliver it by a
          particular date.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Preview access</h2>
        <p>
          The preview shows the product shell with a fictional deal loaded. It is not a trial, it
          is not connected to any environment, and nothing in it saves or executes. Access is
          granted by password to named individuals. Do not share the password, and do not present
          the preview to a third party as a working system.
        </p>
        <p>
          The preview uses the name of a fictional acquirer and a fictional target. Any
          resemblance to a real organisation is unintended.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
          Your use must comply with the <a href="/legal/acceptable-use/">acceptable use policy</a>.
          That policy is part of these terms.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The content, design and code of this site belong to ACQI Technologies or its licensors.
          You may read, print and share pages for the purpose of evaluating the product. You may
          not republish the site, its text or its design as your own, or use the ACQI name or
          marks in a way that suggests endorsement.
        </p>

        <h2>6. No warranty on site content</h2>
        <p>
          The site is provided as it is. We try to keep it correct and available, but we do not
          warrant that it will be uninterrupted, error free, or that every statement remains
          current between updates. The <a href="/status/">status page</a> records that uptime is
          not monitored, and that is an honest limitation rather than a hidden one.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Liability</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing here excludes liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence,
          fraud, or any other liability that cannot be excluded by law.
        </p>
        <p>
          Subject to that, we are not liable for loss of profit, loss of business, loss of
          anticipated savings or indirect loss arising from use of this site. Our total liability
          for any claim connected with the site is limited to one hundred pounds sterling. This
          cap does not apply to a paid licence, which has its own liability terms in the order.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Third-party links</h2>
        <p>
          Where the site links to another organisation, that organisation's terms apply once you
          leave. We are not responsible for its content.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Changes and termination</h2>
        <p>
          We may change the site, withdraw pages that are no longer accurate, or close preview
          access. We may suspend access where these terms or the acceptable use policy are
          breached.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and the courts of England and
          Wales have exclusive jurisdiction. If you are a consumer resident elsewhere, this does
          not remove protections you have under your local law.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms:
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.generalEmail}`}>{SITE.generalEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
